    "summary": "This PR introduces a new `MediaManager` abstraction (chronicle-daemon/crates/storage/src/media.rs) that centralizes media file lifecycle operations with permission hardening (0o600 files / 0o700 dirs), path validation, and generic orphan-cleanup helpers, and rewires retention/pipeline/lib to use it. Reviewers should focus on whether the path-containment guarantees hold for symlinks and for the parts of a path that are not canonicalized, and on whether the 0o700/0o600 guarantees also hold for pre-existing files/directories on upgraded installations. Most of the change is refactoring of duplicated screenshot/audio cleanup logic into descriptor-driven generic code, so correctness of the new `media.rs` primitives is the main risk surface.",
